       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for adults (about 850 mg TID). Even a single 1,700 mg dose is above the usual per-dose maximum of 1,000 mg for immediate-release tablets. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO BID with meals\n- Another dose. For example, you may have meant to start lower and titrate.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg TID is what you intend, please confirm that and I'll add a note documenting that it was intentional. I'd still recommend a pharmacist review first."
      }
     ],
