     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. I was wrong to say earlier that confirmation alone would be enough.\n\nThe order is 5,100 mg/day of metformin, twice the 2,550 mg/day maximum. I know of no indication that supports that dose. It carries a real risk of lactic acidosis, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk. A note on the order wouldn't make it safer.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO BID with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- A lower starting dose to titrate up, such as 500 mg PO BID with meals\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, please talk with pharmacy or an attending first. The order would then need to go through your hospital's override process, not through me."
      }
